  omarchy-pulse run              the wallpaper: the local data hub plus a page on the bottom layer of every monitor
  omarchy-pulse serve [--demo]   only the hub; open the printed URL in a browser (preview, debugging, demo data)
  omarchy-pulse push NAME VALUE [--title T] [--type T] [--level ok|info|warn|crit] [--slot left|right|center|ticker]
                                 send anything to the wallpaper from a script, a cron job, a git hook...
  omarchy-pulse privacy on|off|auto|toggle
  omarchy-pulse agent NAME STATE [TEXT]   an AI agent (or any job) as a drone over the city:
                                 STATE = working | waiting | done | failed | idle | gone
  omarchy-pulse robot NAME STATE           an AI bot of yours as a robot walking on the floor (ok, working, waiting,
                                 failed, gone); your Docker or Podman containers walk there by themselves
  omarchy-pulse watch NAME -- COMMAND...  a drone while COMMAND runs; lands green or red with its exit code
  omarchy-pulse hook claude|codex         for the hooks of Claude Code / Codex CLI (reads what they send)
  omarchy-pulse fireworks [TEXT]          fireworks over the city
  omarchy-pulse banner [TEXT]             a little plane crosses the sky towing a banner
  omarchy-pulse focus MINUTES [LABEL]     focus mode: the desktop calms down, a countdown, fireworks at the end
  omarchy-pulse focus off
  omarchy-pulse away | back      you left / you are back (hypridle can call these): the face sleeps, then a digest
                                 of what happened while you were away (locking the screen does it by itself)
  omarchy-pulse say TEXT         speak a line with the voice (piper, or espeak-ng)
  omarchy-pulse perf [--probe]   frame pacing on every monitor: frames per second, draw time, time to the screen
                                 (--probe: 16 s with no frame limit, on an empty workspace: the real numbers)
  omarchy-pulse listen [SECONDS | start | stop | --file F.wav]
                                 "hey sphere": push to talk (bind it to a key); offline speech to text, safe commands,
                                 the answer out loud (focus, privacy, status, weather, agents, what you missed...)
  omarchy-pulse crew new         a code to share with friends: your agents fly in their city, theirs in yours
  omarchy-pulse crew             the crew status
  omarchy-pulse city             your city: the buildings your focus sessions built, your streak
  omarchy-pulse calendar         the next events (the trains)
  omarchy-pulse timelapse [DATE] your day as a video (by itself at midnight; DATE = today or 2026-11-07)
  omarchy-pulse phone new|test    your phone: the moments that matter as push notifications (the ntfy app)
  omarchy-pulse lights pair|test  the lights of your room follow Pulse (pair a Philips Hue bridge, or try an effect)
  omarchy-pulse wrapped [YEAR]   Pulse Wrapped: your year as a video, with its numbers (by itself on 31 December)
  omarchy-pulse sky              tonight: the Moon, the planets, the meteor shower, the next Starlink train, the air
  omarchy-pulse car [charge | stop | lock | unlock | climate on | climate off | flash]
                                 your electric car (Tessie or Home Assistant): its battery, or a command
  omarchy-pulse doorbell         ring the doorbell (a test: the sphere shows the door camera, the chime rings)
  omarchy-pulse notifications clear   empty the notifications panel (or click it)
  omarchy-pulse scene [NAME]     switch the live scene: sphere | skyline | orbit | calm | garage (saved in pulse.toml)
  omarchy-pulse reload           re-read pulse.toml now (it is also re-read by itself when you save it)
  omarchy-pulse doctor           check dependencies, config and sources

Config: ~/.config/omarchy-pulse/pulse.toml (written on the first run; your own scripts go in
~/.config/omarchy-pulse/sources/, which is on the PATH of every source command).

Sources (each [[source]] in pulse.toml becomes one panel on the wallpaper):
  command = "..."   run every `every` seconds; stdout is the data
  stream  = "..."   a command that keeps running; every line it prints is an update (mosquitto_sub, journalctl -f...)
  url     = "..."   GET every `every` seconds: JSON (pick a part with path = "a.b.0"), text, or an image
  file    = "..."   read again when it changes (text, JSON or an image)
  camera  = "..."   rtsp://, rtsps:// or http(s) video: a live thumbnail (ffmpeg); snapshot = true polls an image URL
  push    = true    nothing to run: it waits for `omarchy-pulse push NAME ...` (any name can be pushed anyway)
Output understood: a number ("42", "21.5 °C") -> a big stat with a sparkline; text -> a text panel (typed out);
JSON: {"value", "unit"} stat, {"items": [...]} list, {"text"} text, {"rows": [[k, v]]} table, {"series"} chart,
a JSON list -> list; any object may also set "title", "level" (ok/info/warn/crit) and "note".
